row.display_mode = Display mode
desc.display_mode = How the game's window is shown. Borderless covers the whole monitor without changing its mode. Exclusive fullscreen takes the monitor for the game alone (it can change how other windows behave).
row.remember_window = Remember window size
desc.remember_window = Opens the window again with the size and place it had when you closed it.
row.vsync = VSync
row.renderer = Renderer
desc.renderer = What draws the game. Vulkan is the default and the faster one here. Direct3D 12 is the older path, kept as a fallback: the game also uses it by itself when Vulkan does not start.
val.vulkan = Vulkan
val.d3d12 = Direct3D 12
desc.vsync = Waits for the monitor before showing each frame. Off can tear the picture, but shows frames as soon as they are ready.
row.show_fps = Show FPS counter
desc.show_fps = A small counter of frames per second in the top right corner while you play.
row.screenshot_key = Screenshot key (F12)
desc.screenshot_key = F12 saves what the window shows to a PNG in your Pictures folder, in ReFine.
timing.early = EARLY
timing.late = LATE
timing.exact = EXACT
timing.mean = mean
note.shot = Screenshot saved
note.shot_failed = Could not save the screenshot
row.pause_focus = Pause on focus lost
desc.pause_focus = Pauses the game with its own pause (START) when its window is no longer in front. Only inside a song.
row.render_height = Internal resolution
desc.render_height = The height of the picture the game is drawn at, then fitted to the window. Higher is sharper and asks more of the graphics card.
row.resampling = Output resampling
desc.resampling = How the picture is fitted to the window when it is bigger. Area removes the shimmer of a big picture shown in a small window.
row.fps_target = Frame rate
desc.fps_target = Real frames drawn each second. The game keeps its original speed at every frame rate; above 30 it looks smoother. Match display uses your monitor's refresh rate, the smoothest choice with V-Sync on. Unlimited draws as fast as your PC can. Any rate from 30 to 1000 can also be set in refine.ini.
row.menu_fps = Menu frame rate
desc.menu_fps = Frame rate of the menus and screens outside songs and PVs. Both keep the original speed. Same as game draws them at the rate above, smoothly, about 33 ms behind your input; 30 draws them as the original. Songs and PVs always use the rate above.
row.best = Choose best for my PC
desc.best = Reads this PC (graphics card, memory, processor, monitor), measures about 5 seconds and proposes a resolution and frame rate that leave at least 30 % of each frame free. Nothing changes until you press Apply.
row.restore = Restore PS3 original
desc.restore = Puts the display mode, VSync, internal resolution and frame rate back to what the PS3 did: a 720p window at 30 frames per second.

row.master_volume = Master volume
desc.master_volume = The volume of everything Re:Fine plays, on top of the game's own volume settings. Applies at once.
row.audio_device = Output device
desc.audio_device = Where the sound goes. Windows default follows the device Windows uses, also when you change it while playing.
row.mute_background = Mute in background
desc.mute_background = No sound while another window is in front.
row.audio_offset = Audio offset
desc.audio_offset = Moves the sound earlier or later to match your speakers or headphones.

row.controller = Controller
desc.controller = The controller the game is reading now. The keyboard always works too.
row.vibration = Vibration
desc.vibration = Lets the controller vibrate when the game asks for it.
row.touch_stars = Touchpad stars
desc.touch_stars = PS4 and PS5 controllers: swipe across the touchpad to hit stars, as a flick of the left stick. On these controllers Share opens this menu and a click on the touchpad is SELECT.
row.star_vibration = Star vibration
desc.star_vibration = A short vibration on each star you hit, and a longer one when a Chance Time ends in success. Not in the PS3 original. Needs Vibration on.
row.mouse_menus = Mouse in game menus
desc.mouse_menus = In the game's menus: wheel moves up and down, left click confirms (Cross), right click goes back (Circle), middle click is Triangle.
row.stick_deadzone = Stick dead zone
desc.stick_deadzone = How far the left stick has to come back to the centre before it counts as released (orange circle). A bigger zone ignores a stick that wobbles near the centre; a smaller one reacts to a lighter touch.
row.stick_hysteresis = Star release threshold
desc.stick_hysteresis = How much further than the dead zone the stick has to go to count as a new flick (green circle). Raise it if one flick gives two stars: the rebound when you let go stays under it.
row.stick_rearm = Star re-arm time
desc.stick_rearm = Time the stick has to stay inside the dead zone before another star can count. Auto is 34 ms above 30 FPS and 0 at 30 FPS.
row.stick_reset = Reset to default
desc.stick_reset = Puts the dead zone, the release threshold and the re-arm time back to their default values.
row.mouse_songs = Mouse in songs
desc.mouse_songs = Lets the mouse buttons and wheel also press during a song. Off: the mouse does nothing while you play.
desc.pad_bind = Press Cross / Enter, then the controller button that will play this PS3 button. Taking one that another button has swaps the two. Square / Delete clears it. Esc, or 5 seconds without a press, cancels.
desc.kb_bind = Each button takes up to two keys. Left / Right choose the first or the second, Cross / Enter waits for the new key. A key used elsewhere moves here. Square / Delete clears it. A controller button, or 5 seconds without a key, cancels.
row.pad_reset = Reset controller buttons
desc.pad_reset = Puts every controller button back where it was at first.
row.kb_reset = Reset keyboard
desc.kb_reset = Puts every key back where it was at first.
bind.press_key = Press a key
bind.press_button = Press a button
note.default = Default: %s
note.bind_taken = Taken from %s, which no longer has it.
note.bind_swapped = Swapped with %s.
