row.timing_display = Timing display
desc.timing_display = Shows how early or late you hit each note, in milliseconds, and the mean of the last 20. It only shows: the judgement does not change.
row.judge_offset = Judgement offset
desc.judge_offset = Moves the timing window of the notes to make up for a slow screen or controller. If the timing display says you hit late on average, raise it by that much. The sound and the picture do not change.
row.skip_intro = Skip Intro Cinematic
desc.skip_intro = Goes to the title screen past the opening movie and what can be skipped of the logos. Applies the next time Re:Fine starts.
row.unlock_all = Unlock all
desc.unlock_all = Unlocks every song, module and item without playing for them.

row.language = Language
desc.language = The language of this menu. More languages come later.
row.menu_scale = Menu scale
desc.menu_scale = Makes this menu bigger or smaller. Applies at once.
row.discord = Discord Rich Presence
desc.discord = Shows the song you are playing on your Discord profile.

row.data_folder = Data folder
desc.data_folder = Where Re:Fine keeps your save data, the settings file (refine.ini) and the shader cache.
row.open_folder = Open data folder
desc.open_folder = Opens the data folder in the Windows file explorer.
row.mods_folder = Mods folder
desc.mods_folder = Each mod goes in its own folder here: a mod.ini (title, author, version, description, game, priority) and its files laid out like the game's USRDIR, for example rom/sound/song/. Mods replace the game's files; they never change them on disk.
row.open_mods = Open mods folder
desc.open_mods = Opens the mods folder in the Windows file explorer (it is made if it is not there yet).
row.mods_none = No mods installed
desc.mods_none = There are no mods in the mods folder. Put a mod's folder there and restart Re:Fine.
desc.mod = When two mods have the same file, the one higher in this list wins (higher priority, then by folder name). Applies after a restart.
mods.by = by
mods.files = files.
mods.priority = Priority
row.backups = Save backups
desc.backups = Every time Re:Fine starts, copies your save data if it changed, and keeps the last 10 copies (the "backups" folder beside your save data).
